; Tutorial_1_User_Interface.inix -- what DbDo is made of, and the rules its keys follow.

[about]
Title=1 - User Interface
Intro=DbDo's window and its parts, each named and then shown by the reader -- the record list, the Say keys, the pick list, the menus -- then the rules every key follows, and help in its four places.
Setup=DbDo is installed, with RadioTrail open, as it is on a first run.
Homework=Guess three DbDo keys from their words, then check each with Control plus F1.

[step]

Say=DbDo is heard before it is seen. I name each part; the reader shows it: name, kind, value and state, then a hint.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=The title, then the greeting in the message voice. The main view is a list of records: Down Arrow moves by row, and the reader speaks the record.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=(the next record, its first column first)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Right Arrow moves by column within the record, speaking the column's name and its value.
Key=Right Arrow
Hear=(the next column's name and value)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Now the Say keys: Shift and a letter asks, and changes nothing. Shift plus Z is Say Status.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=jobs, 12 records, no filter, sorted by employer

[step]

Say=Table, count, filter and sort in one breath; pressed twice, the words open in a window. Shift plus C, C for Cell, says the cell you are on.
Key=Shift+C
Hear=(the column's name and the cell's value)
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Where a field has fixed values, F4 opens them as a pick list.
Key=F4
Hear=status: list box, untried, 4 of 5
Hear=To move through items press Up or Down Arrow.

[step]

Say=A letter jumps to a value, so nothing is mistyped. Escape closes it. Menus say their own keys; F10 opens the menu bar.
Key=F10
Hear=Menu bar
Hear=File menu

[step]

Say=Down Arrow to the first item.
Key=Down Arrow
Hear=Open Database..., Control plus O, O

[step]

Say=The item, its key, then its letter: learn a key from the menu once, then skip the menu.
Key=Escape
Hear=Leaving menus

[step]

Say=The rules behind every key. A letter is the first letter of a word: Control plus O opens, Alt plus O orders. Control does; Shift asks, changing nothing.
Key=Shift+Z
Hear=jobs, 12 records, no filter, sorted by employer
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Adding Shift reverses: Control plus M marks, Control plus Shift plus M unmarks. Each function key is a family: F2 edits, F3 searches, F4 picks, F8 selects. Insert plus T, the reader's own, says the title.
Key=Insert+T
Hear=DbDo

[step]

Say=Control plus F1 is the Key Describer: each key says what it does instead of doing it.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=Key Describer On

[step]

Say=Again, and it is off.
Key=Control+F1
Hear=No Key Describer

[step]

Say=Help is in four places, the same in every Homer program. I say which; the reader says the key. The guide.
Key=
Hear=F1, the guide

[step]

Say=The changes, release by release; the version; the name of any key.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus F1, History
Hear=Alt plus F1, About
Hear=Control plus F1, Key Describer

[step]

Say=When a key will not come to mind, Alt plus F10, the Alternate Menu, lists every command in one list you type into, with its key beside it.
Key=Alt+F10
Hear=Alternate Menu
Hear=Command, list box
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type the word mark, and the list narrows to the commands with that word.
Key=mark
Hear=Mark All, Control plus A
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes the list without running anything.
Key=Escape
Hear=jobs, 12 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Say Status.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus Z

[step]

Say=A field's fixed values.
Key=
Hear=F4, pick list

[step]

Say=Unmark, the reverse of Mark.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Shift plus M
